    {
      "id": 264058,
      "name": "",
      "username": "LonelyMan",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/l/f4b2a3/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2025-10-15T13:11:59.016Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Normal universe The Master is an Asian occultist dude, Zhang I think he’s named, and we don’t seem to get the good version of him, nor of Zhu Long   With Slim Walker being far older than his original version, Zhu Long could be younger, and Zhang could be his sidekick.</p>\n<p>A big thing that’s missing from all of these Inversiverse stories is what happens during OblivAeon.  I like the idea that, for instance, Action Hero Stuntman turns into a “villain”, not in the sense that he’s evil and hunting heroes for sport, but more like Tachyon in the Bloodsworn Coliseum, where he realizes the rules of this conflict require a sacrifice play, and thus he becomes a Deadline-like anti-hero, killing people who would have caused problems, and ultimately losing his soul in the defeat of OA.</p>",
      "post_number": 8,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2025-10-15T13:58:40.259Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
